  "visualBrief": "The Barlow train shed has one broad glazed vault above raised platforms, set against a low modern northern extension. The red-brick Midland Grand frontage adds a recessed entrance, stepped Gothic roofs and the Euston Road clock tower.",
  "heightPolicy": "The 17 m sea-level datum follows standard viewer terrain at the streets. The raised station deck has a stepped apron and open north underpass. The two named building outlines replace the station and adjoining hotel, along with three contained elevator parts.",
  "nativeAxes": "+X runs southeast from the north rail approach and modern roof to the hotel and Euston Road; +Z faces the British Library side.",
  "limitations": [
    "The station and adjoining hotel footprints and the platform edges come from PMTiles. The Barlow roof heights, rail level, Gothic frontage and towers are reconstructed from exterior and train-shed photographs, with standard terrain for street contact.",
    "Visible platforms and station elevator volumes are represented. Track centerlines are estimated between mapped platform edges. Hotel interiors and operations below the raised station deck are outside the reconstruction."
  ],
